      "hints": [
        "Substitute the $R$-form expression into the integrand and express $\\dfrac{1}{\\cos^2(2x + \\pi/6)}$ as $\\sec^2(2x + \\pi/6)$.",
        "Integrate $\\sec^2(2x + \\pi/6)$ to obtain $\\dfrac{1}{2}\\tan(2x + \\pi/6)$, and evaluate between $x = 0$ and $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Substitute $3\\cos(2x) - \\sqrt{3}\\sin(2x) = 2\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$ into the integral:\n$$\\int_0^{\\pi/12} \\dfrac{3}{\\left(2\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right)^2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\int_0^{\\pi/12} \\dfrac{3}{12\\cos^2\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$$",
        "Simplify the integrand and write in terms of $\\sec^2$:\n$$\\dfrac{3}{12\\cos^2\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sec^2\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$$",
        "Integrate using $\\int \\sec^2(kx + c)\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{k}\\tan(kx + c)$ with $k = 2$:\n$$\\int \\dfrac{1}{4}\\sec^2\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\tan\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)\\right) = \\dfrac{1}{8}\\tan\\left(2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right)$$",
        "Evaluate at the upper limit $x = \\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$:\n$$2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = 2\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$$\n$$\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right) = \\sqrt{3}$$\n$$\\text{Upper} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\\sqrt{3} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{8}$$",
        "Evaluate at the lower limit $x = 0$:\n$$2x + \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$$\n$$\\tan\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}\\right) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$$\n$$\\text{Lower} = \\dfrac{1}{8}\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\right) = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{24}$$",
        "Subtract lower limit from upper limit:\n$$\\text{Integral} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} - \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{24} = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{24} - \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{24} = \\dfrac{2\\sqrt{3}}{24} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{12}$$\n$$\\left(\\text{or } \\dfrac{1}{4\\sqrt{3}}\\right)$$"
      ],
